## 3. Required source notices

### Copernicus Sentinel-derived label data

The three `consensus_label.tif` files are modified Sentinel-2 Level-2A-derived
labels. The source notices are:

- `Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data 2022` (Pohang)
- `Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data 2023` (Yecheon)
- `Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data 2020` (Chuncheon)

Official legal notice:
https://sentinels.copernicus.eu/documents/247904/690755/Sentinel_Data_Legal_Notice

### Forest-service administrative-unit statistics

`brief_communication_reproducibility/data/frozen_tables/unit_level_stats.csv`
is derived from `산림청_과거산사태 정보`, provided by the Korea Forest
Service through data.go.kr, dataset ID 15074816:

https://www.data.go.kr/data/15074816/openapi.do

The official dataset page states `이용허락범위 제한 없음`. It does not show a
dataset-specific Kogl mark or a mandatory attribution sentence; none is
invented here.

### Copernicus DEM GLO-30 regeneration route

The source DEM tiles and the derived terrain raster are not distributed in the
file set licensed above. For regeneration, the applicable modified-data notice
is:

`produced using Copernicus WorldDEM-30 © DLR e.V. 2010-2014 and © Airbus Defence and Space GmbH 2014-2018 provided under COPERNICUS by the European Union and ESA; all rights reserved`

The required no-liability sentence is:

`The organisations in charge of the Copernicus programme by law or by delegation do not incur any liability for any use of the Copernicus WorldDEM-30`.

No official endorsement by the provider, licensor, European Union, ESA, or any
other entity in charge of the Copernicus programme is expressed or implied.

The Copernicus WorldDEM-30 is made available to the Users 'as is'. The User
uses it under its own responsibility.

Official GLO-30 licence:
https://documentation.dataspace.copernicus.eu/APIs/SentinelHub/Data/DEM/resources/license/License-COPDEM-30.pdf

